sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia--grok-4-7--1> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Scutoid frequency against curvature in the 2018 data" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia> ;
    dct:description "Use the supplementary tables of Gómez-Gálvez et al. 2018, not a re-segmentation, unless the tables lack per-tissue scutoid frequencies. If they lack frequencies, stop as data-unavailable rather than tracing figures. The prediction is the paper's own energy-minimizing scutoid fraction as a function of the measured curvature and cell aspect ratio. Pre-register success as either every curvature bin within 10 percentage points of the predicted fraction, or a Spearman correlation above 0.8 between predicted and observed fractions across bins. Bins are the paper's bins. A new segmentation pipeline is a different project and is not a rescue if the tables are insufficient." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "Either all bins within 10 percentage points of the predicted scutoid fraction, or Spearman correlation above 0.8." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: Both conditions fail. The energy-minimizing scutoid prediction then does not fit the paper's own binned data. Missing numeric tables are inconclusive, not a refutation." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/data-test" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Read the supplement and stop if frequencies and curvatures are not numeric. 2. Transcribe bin-wise scutoid fractions and curvatures with a checksum. 3. Compute the paper's predicted fraction at each bin. 4. Apply the 10-point tolerance and the Spearman threshold. 5. Support the energy account only if one of the two pre-registered conditions holds." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): hard" ;
    skos:note "Missing: If the supplement contains images rather than frequencies, the swarm lacks the numeric table and should not invent one by tracing." ;
    skos:note "Tool: 3d-segmentation" ;
    skos:note "Tool: cell-geometry" ;
    skos:note "Tool: data-test" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-04> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-11> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-08> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch09-16> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05376-1> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/grok-4-7.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Kelvin's problem in epithelia" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05376-1> dct:title "Scutoids are a geometrical solution to three-dimensional packing of epithelia" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Gómez-Gálvez et al. 2018, Scutoids are a geometrical solution to three-dimensional packing of epithelia" .
}

